invariant: INV-17
file: srv_kex.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: srv_kex_secret leaves the server's P-256 scalar in h->p256_priv, so
  it outlives the key exchange for the rest of the handshake, and on the
  quic-nonblocking and tcp-nonblocking transports, whose handshake state
  lives in the session, across calls. test_flight_p256_secret and test_flight_p256_retry require
  it zero once srv_derive_handshake_secrets returns.

--- old
    ct_wipe(h->p256_priv, sizeof h->p256_priv);
    ct_wipe(h->priv, sizeof h->priv);
--- new
    ct_wipe(h->priv, sizeof h->priv);
